# First-party, not a plugin internal: tracked `ccu.fish` calls it, so a fresh
# clone without it has a broken `ccu`.
!fish/functions/_claude_release_notes.fish
# Same: cc-worktree isolation. These MUST be their own files because fish
# autoloads by filename, and `_cc_worktree_key` runs on every `cd` (chpwd ->
# _ccs_open_scan) and inside `fish -c` subshells, so it cannot live inside
# ccs.fish. Without these lines a fresh clone gets a ccs that keys every
# isolated session to the worktree, and a wrapper that cannot resolve a slot.
!fish/functions/_cc_worktree_key.fish
!fish/functions/_cc_worktree_slot.fish
!fish/functions/__cc_resume_id.fish
!fish/functions/__cc_resume_requested.fish
